>> C2: Describe how memory mapped files integrate into your virtual
>> memory subsystem.  Explain how the page fault and eviction
>> processes differ between swap pages and other pages.

I create vm_entries until they covers the whole mmap_file. And then,
allocates the page when the page fault occurs.
When page fault or eviction occurs, swap pages use swap_in/out() functions
to load/store data from/to the swap space, but mmap file load/store data by
reading/writing file using file system call.

